## CI policy (DND-2.3+)

- Feature → develop: full **local** quality gate; GitHub CI not required / should not run.
- Develop → master: GitHub `promote-gate` + `quality` must run and pass before merge.
- After FX.6: the full Playwright Chromium / Firefox / WebKit matrix is mandatory **locally** before pushing `develop`. GitHub `browser-e2e` remains a named status / manual dispatch job and does not reinstall browsers or rerun that matrix on promotion.

## Hard exclusions (until an explicit sprint requires them)

Cursor MUST NOT introduce:

- New AI provider SDKs / Gemini / Anthropic / local model runtimes / network-required intelligence as **public** product paths (model assistance deferred; DND-4.4 OpenAI reference already exists privately — do not expand or publish without authorization)
- **Public** `@dndgem/intelligence` or `@dndgem/intelligence-openai` packages / npm publication (private workspace packages already exist as authorized reference architecture; do not promote them)
- Flutter implementation (separate track; not a DND-FX sprint)
- Vue adapter expansion beyond closed DND-FX.2 unless an explicit follow-up authorizes it
- Angular adapter expansion beyond closed DND-FX.3 unless an explicit follow-up authorizes it
- Svelte adapter expansion beyond closed DND-FX.4 unless an explicit follow-up authorizes it
- `@dndgem/next`, `@dndgem/nuxt`, `@dndgem/sveltekit`, `@dndgem/framework-core`, `@dndgem/vanilla`, `@dndgem/ai` packages
- Placeholder / stub packages to reserve names
- Pin / Lock / fixed / manual placement APIs (deferred unless a sprint explicitly requires them)
- cloud services / billing / Stripe
- Layout CI SaaS / team accounts / enterprise functionality
- custom native DnD engine
- npm publication / repository visibility changes unless the active sprint explicitly requires it
- Broader-than-minimal Public Auto-Layout API freeze unless an explicit review requires it
- Second solver / parallel validity vocabulary / intelligence inside Core by default
- Publishing npm, mutating dist-tags, changing package versions, or starting a new release without an explicitly authorized release gate

DND-FX.2 is **COMPLETE**. DND-FX.3 is **COMPLETE**. DND-FX.4 is **COMPLETE**. DND-FX.6 originally closed the cross-framework release at `0.1.0-alpha.3`; adapters remain on the current public Alpha channel (`0.1.0-alpha.4` / `@alpha`). Do not implement SvelteKit / Nuxt / Next packages. DND-FX.5 is **COMPLETE** (private compatibility fixtures; dedicated meta-framework packages not required). DND-FX.6 is **COMPLETE**. DND-FX.1 remains closed. Do not reopen Framework Expansion except for an authorized follow-up.

Flutter compatibility may be considered architecturally (types, ADRs), but not implemented until scheduled.

Intelligence is optional and outside the critical deterministic path; Phase 4 shipped deterministic planner surfaces in `0.1.0-alpha.4`. Preferred home: optional intelligence layer depending on Core (ADR-0018), not framework adapters.

Repository identity is **public open source** (`davideagosti-dev/dndgem`). GitHub visibility flip (PRIVATE → PUBLIC) requires an explicit Product Owner Visibility Gate — do not change visibility without that authorization.

Public Alpha installs must use **`@alpha`** (`0.1.0-alpha.4` is the current official public Alpha). Do not document bare / `latest` installs as the supported Alpha path.

`0.1.0-alpha.4` is released and closed. No Alpha.5 or Phase 5 work is authorized by this governance sync. The next roadmap/release step requires a separate explicit planning gate.

## Phase 3 binding refinements

- Auto-Layout enrichs intent; existing `solveLayout` remains the only selection/validity authority.
- Source intent vs generated/effective placement provenance must stay distinguishable.
- Drag produces strong persistent user intent, not an absolute immutable pin.
- Auto-Layout remains opt-in for Phase 3 Alpha (default off).
- Minimal public enricher API approved (DND-3.4): `createAutoLayoutProposal` + types; DOM/React `autoLayout`. Broader freeze remains an explicit review / later decision; DND-3.5 published the minimal surface as `0.1.0-alpha.1`.
- Previous layout is stability-only input to Auto-Layout proposals; it is never an origin and never Source Intent.

## Framework Expansion binding refinements

- JS/DOM adapters are thin over `createLayoutSession` (ADR-0015).
- React / Vue / Angular / Svelte are siblings over `@dndgem/dom` (ADR-0016).
- Next.js / Nuxt / SvelteKit are compatibility environments, not packages (ADR-0017).
- Framework adapters must not become AI extension points.

## Phase 4 binding refinements (DND-4.1 → DND-4.5)

- Intelligence proposes; deterministic DnDGem validates and resolves.
- `solveLayout` / `evaluateLayout` remain the only validity/scoring/resolution authority.
- Phase 4 does not require an LLM; heuristic/deterministic planner is the preferred first implementation (DND-4.2 — COMPLETE / RELEASED in `0.1.0-alpha.4`).
- Provider-neutral planner boundary required; no production provider selected; DND-4.4 deferred model assistance until new evidence.
- Planning Proposals are UNTRUSTED until validated/normalized; fail closed to deterministic fallback.
- No model inference in hot paths (pointermove / rAF / ResizeObserver / every solve).
- Privacy by default: structural/serializable payloads only unless explicit consumer opt-in.
- Accessibility ownership remains with the consumer; intelligence must not auto-rewrite DOM/read/tab/ARIA semantics.
- Deterministic DnDGem may progress toward Beta independently of model-based intelligence.
- Existing private `@dndgem/intelligence` / `@dndgem/intelligence-openai` are authorized reference packages; public publication is not authorized.
- Phase 4 is **COMPLETE AND SHIPPED** in `0.1.0-alpha.4`. DND-4.3 planner integration is **COMPLETE / RELEASED** in `0.1.0-alpha.4`. No Alpha.5 or Phase 5 work is authorized without a separate explicit planning gate.
